Drive-feedback 159/15a ("too early and too hard"; 85/89 gas-ended episodes cancelled
mid-brake). The deployed (OLD-LAW) path only ever emitted {0, 4, 8..20} LSB. That is
the law, not the wire: CR_VSM_DecCmd is an 8-bit 0.01 g integer and the panda accepts
any level <= +RATE_STEP over the last accepted frame. The -0.5 onset maps through the
0.67 inverse to 8, the release band clamps the ask to -0.5 (floor 8), and the limiter
goes 0 -> 4 -> 8 in 40 ms - straight into the plant's worst over-delivery (L=8 ~1.2
m/s^2, 1.5-2x nominal), 0.28 s lag and 0.53 s release tail.

0049 adds a feel layer on the OLD-LAW instance only (not the shaping/V3 law, not cal,
not the <=3 km/h hold band, which run exactly as before):
  * coast-first open at ask <= -0.60 (coast 0.15 + margin 0.45); release rule unchanged
    (hysteresis); HARD asks (<= -1.2) open on frame 1; a small ask sustained <= -0.5 for
    1.0 s opens anyway (dwell escape);
  * onset ramp: first frame 4, then jerk-limited growth (2.5 m/s^3 through the
    per-level delivered slope; the 4-8 band slope is PROVISIONAL) blending to the full
    +RATE_STEP at -1.2; an ask deepening faster than -2 m/s^3 also gets +RATE_STEP;
  * anticipatory release: while the ask eases, the target uses the ask 0.28 s ahead
    (capped 0.25 m/s^2), and the release band follows the 0.67 inverse down through
    7/6/5/4 instead of clamping at 8. The exit frame and passive close are unchanged.

Authority: the requested level is never above the deployed request for the same ask;
the steady level for asks <= -0.5 is unchanged; a hard ask from idle is byte-identical.
Disclosed trade: soft->hard can reach the cap up to ~3 sent frames later. Panda
contract, passive close on every exit, R7 latch, camera hand-back, arming, the
shadow log schema: untouched. FCA11_FEEL_ENABLED=False is byte-identical to 0048
(proven over the three recorded drives x three personalities). No param / CP_SP field
in this patch (module constants; a runtime param needs a coordinated capnp change).

Tests: test_fca11_feel.py (30) + all existing fca11 tests (274) green; 16/16 guard
mutations killed. Offline replay (open-loop, routes 158/159/15a): onset command jerk
p50 4.91 -> 2.45 m/s^3; 12 of 131 episodes not opened.
